    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_battery_help">Could not verify the Android battery optimization exemption for xDrip+. Open the app battery settings and check restrictions manually. An exemption does not cover all manufacturer-specific background limits.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_autostart_help">Autostart is managed by some phone manufacturers, and Android has no universal way to read its state. xDrip+ tries a read-only check on supported Xiaomi systems. If the status is unknown, enable autostart manually in system settings. On Xiaomi, look under Settings → Apps → Permissions → Autostart (names may vary).</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_bluetooth_help">Could not check Bluetooth. Open Android Bluetooth settings and turn it on manually. This is a system switch, not permission to change it silently. Individual sensor routes can require additional permissions.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_location_help">Location readiness checks xDrip+ location access (including background access where the existing Bluetooth helper requires it) and the system Location switch. If app permission is missing, Fix opens Android app settings: Permissions → Location; choose Allow all the time if available and needed. If the system Location switch is off, Fix opens Location settings. Some Bluetooth routes do not require location; this general check never blocks source selection.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_allow">Allow</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_location_permission_steps_background">To receive data in the background, xDrip+ needs location access.\n\nIn the system settings that open:\n1. Tap “App permissions” (or “Permissions”).\n2. Select “Location”.\n3. Choose “Allow all the time” (or the equivalent option).\n4. Return to xDrip+ — the status will refresh automatically.\n\nMenu names vary between phones. “Allow” opens settings; you grant access there.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_location_permission_steps_foreground">To use location for compatible connections, grant location access to xDrip+.\n\nIn the system settings that open:\n1. Tap “App permissions” (or “Permissions”).\n2. Select “Location”.\n3. Allow location access.\n4. Return to xDrip+ — the status will refresh automatically.\n\n“Allow” opens settings; you grant access there.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_location_settings_unavailable">Could not open app settings. Open Android Settings → Apps → xDrip+ → Permissions → Location manually.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_readiness_pin_help">xDrip+ cannot reliably detect whether it is locked in the recent-apps list. Open recent apps and lock xDrip+ using a padlock control, if your phone provides one. This is different from Android screen pinning.</string>
