    <string name="source_wizard_follower_about">How it works</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_follower_carelink_body">xDrip+ receives glucose readings uploaded to the Medtronic CareLink cloud by compatible Guardian 3/4, Simplera or MiniMed 7xxG systems. It does not connect directly to the sensor. A supported CareLink account, internet access and glucose data uploaded to CareLink are required. Readings may be delayed; availability varies by region and configuration.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_follower_dexshare_body">xDrip+ reads glucose data from Dexcom Share. Sharing must be enabled for the supported Dexcom system, and you need authorized access to its Share data. Service availability depends on the account and region.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_follower_nightscout_body">xDrip+ downloads readings from your Nightscout server. You need a working Nightscout address and permission to read its data. Glucose readings must already be uploaded to Nightscout.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_follower_web_body">xDrip+ reads glucose data from a supported web service. Choose the provider and sign in as needed in the source settings. Available integrations depend on the service.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_follower_xdrip_body">This phone receives glucose readings from another xDrip+ installation via xDrip Sync. First configure data sharing on the sending phone, then connect this follower.</string>
